# NOTE: this file must stay UTF-8. It has been saved as UTF-16 four times now,
# and git cannot parse UTF-16 at all -- every rule below goes silently inert and
# .pyc files start getting committed. Do not "fix" it in an editor that re-saves
# as UTF-16/UCS-2 (PowerShell `>` redirection and Set-Content both default to
# UTF-16LE on Windows; use `Set-Content -Encoding utf8`, or Notepad's
# "Save as -> UTF-8").
#
# To verify the rules are actually live:
#     git check-ignore -v __pycache__/anything.pyc     # must print a matching rule
#     file .gitignore                                  # must NOT say UTF-16
#
# The fourth recurrence had already landed when this was rewritten: `file` said
# UTF-16LE, check-ignore matched nothing, and 12 .pyc files were tracked. If you
# are reading this because it happened again, the durable fix is a pre-commit
# hook or a .gitattributes entry, not another manual re-save.

# virtualenvs
akira_env/
sensei_env/
.venv/

# python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# secrets / credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
credentials.json
token.json
memory/.session_vault.key
memory/*.vault
memory/*.key
*.procedures.key
.procedures.key

# temporary office lock files & test artifacts
~$*
tests/*_results.json

# models
*.onnx
*.onnx.data
*.gguf
*.bin
Akira/

# drivers
chromedriver-win64/
chromedriver.exe

# scratch & test artifacts
test.py
.v0/
scratch/
*.mp3

# Diagnostic/debug artifacts — not meant for version control
akira_system_prompts_dump.md
live_all_local_functions_report.json
live_function_test_results.json
live_verified_report.json
akira_performance_dashboard.html
*.db
procedures.db
.procedures.key
*.procedures.key
voice_engine_branch/
memory/logs/